11. Role of ServiceNow MCP

Management suggested exploring ServiceNow MCP servers. This is a valid recommendation.

MCP should be evaluated as an integration layer, not as a full replacement for ARCA.

MCP can help ARCA read ServiceNow data in a governed way. Instead of building every ServiceNow API integration from scratch, an MCP server may expose approved tools for reading change details, tasks, assignment information, and approval state.

Potential MCP tools:

get_change_details(change_number)
get_change_tasks(change_number)
get_change_approvals(change_number)
get_change_implementer(change_number)
get_change_window(change_number)
get_change_ci_or_resource(change_number)
get_change_work_notes(change_number)

For the recommended Phase 1 design, MCP should be read-only.

MCP should not expose update or approval tools initially.

Allowed:
Read change details
Read related tasks
Read planned start/end
Read implementer
Read approval state
Read work notes if required

Not allowed in Phase 1:
Update change records
Approve changes
Reject changes
Create PIM requests
Approve PIM requests
Modify ServiceNow work notes automatically

Recommended MCP positioning:
ServiceNow MCP can be used as a read-only integration layer for retrieving change context. ARCA’s core validation and risk-analysis engine remains independent from the integration method.

This means ARCA can work with:

* ServiceNow MCP
* ServiceNow REST API
* ServiceNow webhook
* ServiceNow Flow Designer
* Manual input for prototype/demo

12. Why MCP Does Not Replace ARCA

MCP can expose ServiceNow data and actions, but it does not automatically implement the company’s privileged-access policy.

MCP does not automatically know:

* Whether Contributor is too broad
* Whether Subscription scope is justified
* Whether the requested duration matches the change window
* Whether the PIM requester matches the approved implementer
* Which Azure RBAC actions are required for the change
* Which least-privilege role should be recommended
* Whether the change description has enough access details
* Whether the PIM request creates access risk

These are ARCA’s responsibilities.

Therefore, the correct architecture is:

ServiceNow MCP / REST / Webhook
↓
ARCA Validation Engine
↓
Azure RBAC / PIM Data
↓
Risk Analysis and Recommendation
↓
Approver / Dashboard / ServiceNow Display Channel

MCP is an integration enabler. ARCA is the intelligence and decision-support engine.

