21. Why Azure OpenAI for Enterprise

The local prototype used a local model and local runtime to prove the concept. At enterprise level, ARCA should use Azure OpenAI or Microsoft Foundry model deployment because it provides enterprise-grade governance.

Benefits:

* Company-approved AI platform
* Better security controls
* Private networking support
* Identity and access management
* Monitoring and logging
* Scalable model deployment
* Better operational support
* Easier integration with Azure services
* Central governance for AI usage

Recommended LLM usage:
Use the LLM for extraction, classification, summarization, and explanation.

Do not use the LLM as the final approval authority.

The final recommendation should come from deterministic rule logic, Azure RBAC role definitions, action mappings, and policy rules.

22. Why Final Decision Should Not Be Fully LLM-Based

For security and privileged access use cases, explainability is critical.

A poor design would be:

Change text
↓
LLM directly says approve or reject

This is risky because LLMs can hallucinate, be inconsistent, or provide confident but incorrect recommendations.

Recommended design:

Change text
↓
LLM extracts structured fields
↓
Rule engine maps required actions
↓
RBAC engine checks role coverage
↓
Decision engine compares requested vs recommended access
↓
Human approver takes final action

This keeps ARCA explainable, auditable, and safer.

