32. Short Management-Friendly Explanation

ARCA expands the current prototype into a two-stage change-to-access risk analyzer. In the first stage, ARCA automatically validates the quality of ServiceNow changes when they move out of Draft or reach a configured workflow stage. It checks whether the change contains enough information for access-risk review, such as resource, environment, implementer, access need, scope, and time window.

In the second stage, ARCA assists privileged-access approvers by comparing the approved change against the actual PIM request. It validates whether the requested role, scope, duration, implementer, and justification match the approved change. ARCA provides evidence-based recommendations such as approve recommended, reject overprivileged, scope mismatch, duration mismatch, implementer mismatch, or manual review required.

ARCA will operate in read-only advisory mode. It will not directly update ServiceNow records or approve/reject PIM requests. This makes the solution safer to introduce and easier to govern while still improving access-risk visibility and decision quality.

33. Short Technical Explanation

ARCA uses an enterprise AI-assisted architecture where an LLM extracts structured information from unstructured change descriptions. The final access-risk recommendation is not directly decided by the LLM. Instead, deterministic services map change intent to required Azure RBAC actions, compare those actions against Azure role definitions, and validate whether the actual PIM request aligns with the approved change.

The enterprise version can use Azure OpenAI for extraction and classification, ServiceNow webhook or MCP for change data retrieval, Microsoft Graph or Azure APIs for PIM request details, and a rule-based decision engine for role, scope, duration, and implementer validation.

This hybrid design combines the flexibility of AI for understanding change text with the reliability of deterministic access-control logic for security decisions.

34. Final One-Line Summary

ARCA — Access Risk & Change Analyzer — is a read-only advisory platform that validates change quality early and helps PIM approvers confirm whether privileged access requests align with approved changes, reducing overprivilege and improving access governance.

